- Deferred by the user: consolidate document metadata in `mobile-document-route.ts`, `../ProjectView.tsx`, and `../routing/` around one route-admitted presentation; remove the secondary document catalog lookup and redundant retention fields only after local Untitled, viewer, Work and draft-review paths are covered. Preserve phone's distinct UI, single-active-view lifecycle and session-host ownership; do not unify it with desktop. Add phone composition-level transition coverage and a real phone probe. Implementation sequence and acceptance criteria: [#529](https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow/issues/529). Not part of PR #526's current implementation scope.
- `MobileBreadcrumb.tsx`: the `…` of an elided trail is inert, a dead control on the phone's only path. Decide what it opens (the path decision opens one level above the crumb after it) and make it a tap target, or stop eliding the folders it hides. The phone shell does not render the desktop path bar ([KB: path decision](https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow-docs/blob/main/kb/decisions/writer-ux/interaction/documents/path-navigates-lists-edit.md)).
- `MobileContextBrowser.tsx`: Move… shares the desktop `EntryMovePicker`, but was never exercised in a real coarse-pointer phone shell (browser emulation kept dropping the coarse pointer). Verify the picker's anchoring, 44px targets, refused-move retry and the "Moved to <folder>" note on a phone, and add it to a phone probe.
